{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1107020185#1_2331556541","relevance":3,"reason":"The Forbes article is dedicated to phishing and directly explains that attackers use social engineering to take advantage of human curiosity, fear, and gullibility to manipulate victims, which directly supports what it means for a cybercrime to appeal to a victim.","learned":"Phishing appeals to victims by exploiting traits and emotions such as curiosity, fear, and gullibility to manipulate them into acting."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991","reason":"This result set continues to provide direct grade-3 explanations of how cybercrime manipulates victims through psychological and emotional appeals, so continue."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1107020185#2_2331558073","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1991","rank":4,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1107020185#2_2331558073\" , \"end_char\": 2673.000000 , \"headings\": \"The Dangers Of Phishing The Dangers Of Phishing Ricardo Villadiego How Did This Happen? Phishing Causes Permanent Damage To Brands \" , \"segment\": \"Fast-forward to Monday morning’s news headlines: Your company and your client have fallen victim to a massive phishing scheme. How Did This Happen? Phishing is all about the art of deception. Through <cover>social engineering, attackers take advantage human curiosity, fear and gullibility to manipulate their victims. </cover>In the case above, the hypothetical attacker took advantage of someone's fear of being compromised in order to actually compromise them. While phishing attacks have traditionally included emails spread across a wide group of organizations, spear phishing -- which targets a specific person or group of people -- has become more common. These targeted attacks are more efficient and sophisticated since they involve extensive planning and research about the victims. 2016 saw a 65% increase in phishing, with a total of 1,220,523 attacks for the year. This points to a much larger number "}}
