{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1107020185#2_2331558073","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of the Forbes phishing article already seen, but it still directly states that phishing uses social engineering to exploit curiosity, fear, and gullibility to manipulate victims, which is direct evidence for what it means for cybercrime to appeal to a victim.","learned":"Targeted phishing appeals to victims by researching them and exploiting fear or other human traits to manipulate them."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991","reason":"Continue this productive result set, while watching for non-duplicate documents with direct explanations of victim appeals and psychological manipulation."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_1393709560#7_2901318458","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1991","rank":5,"snippet":"A spear phishing scenario might involve an attacker who, in impersonating an organization’s IT consultant, sends an email to one or more employees. It’s worded and signed exactly as the consultant normally does, thereby deceiving recipients into thinking it’s an authentic message. The message prompts recipients to change their password and provides them with a link that redirects them to a malicious page where the attacker now captures their credentials. See how Imperva Web Application Firewall can help you with social engineering attacks. Request Demo learn more<cover>Social engineering prevention Social engineers manipulate human feelings, such as curiosity or fear, to carry out schemes and draw victims </cover>into their traps. Therefore, be wary whenever you feel alarmed by an email, attracted to an offer displayed on a website, or when you come across stray digital media lying about. Being alert can help you protect yourself against most social engineering attacks taking place in the digital realm.\" , \"start_char\": 5107.000000 , \"title\": \"What is Social Engineering | Attack Techniques & Prevention Methods | Imperva\" , \"url\": \"https://www.imperva.com/learn/application-security/social-"}}
