{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_573680833#7_1162271836","relevance":3,"reason":"The result is dedicated to common social engineering attacks and directly explains that attackers build trust and manipulate victims into actions, with baiting exploiting human curiosity, which supports what it means for a cybercrime to appeal to a victim.","learned":"Appealing to a victim can involve creating a trusted pretext or bait that exploits curiosity so the victim performs an action useful to the attacker."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991","reason":"This result set is still yielding direct evidence about psychological manipulation, trust, and emotions in cybercrime, so continue for more grade-3 documents."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_43_1393709560#8_2901320416","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1991","rank":7,"snippet":"headings\": \"Social Engineering Social Engineering What is social engineering Social engineering attack techniques Baiting Scareware Pretexting Phishing Spear phishing See how Imperva Web Application Firewall can help you with social engineering attacks. Social engineering prevention \" , \"segment\": \"The message prompts recipients to change their password and provides them with a link that redirects them to a malicious page where the attacker now captures their credentials. See how Imperva Web Application Firewall can help you with social engineering attacks. Request Demo learn more<cover>Social engineering prevention Social engineers manipulate human feelings, such as curiosity or fear, to carry out schemes and draw victims </cover>into their traps. Therefore, be wary whenever you feel alarmed by an email, attracted to an offer displayed on a website, or when you come across stray digital media lying about. Being alert can help you protect yourself against most social engineering attacks taking place in the digital realm. Moreover, the following tips can help improve your vigilance in relation to social engineering hacks. Don’t open emails and attachments from suspicious sources – If you don’t know the sender in question, you don’t need to answer an email. "}}
