{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1588958815#3_3284524925","relevance":3,"reason":"The result is dedicated to whaling/phishing techniques and directly explains that attackers use realistic emails and psychological manipulation, preying on emotions such as uncertainty, greed, fear, and urgency to make the victim accept the message and take harmful actions.","learned":"Cybercrime can appeal to a victim by making a lure look normal and trustworthy while exploiting the victim's stress, uncertainty, greed, fear, or urgency."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991","reason":"The current social-engineering result set is still yielding direct grade-3 evidence about psychological and emotional appeals to victims, so continue for more relevant documents."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1991"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1246643094#5_2667010111","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1991","rank":21,"snippet":"some other kind of malware. Pretexting In an attack that uses pretexting, the attacker lies to the victim regarding their identity. After they have gained the target’s trust, they trick them into handing over sensitive information. Phishing In a phishing attack, the attacker creates a sense of urgency or appeals to the victim’s curiosity. They then either get them to click on a malicious link or provide private information via a form. Spear Phishing With a spear-phishing attack, the victim is specifically targeted, and the attacker often performs extensive research ahead of time. Once the attacker knows how to <cover>manipulate the victim, they launch the attack, phishing for information, credentials, or sensitive data. Water Holing With water holing, the attacker tries to compromise a targeted group of individuals by infecting sites they trust. The attacker may focus on sites that the people visit frequently, knowing they are likely to feel safe on those pages.\" , \"start_char\": 2994.000000 , \"title\": \"What Is Social Engineering? </cover>Preventing Social Engineering Attacks | Fortinet\" , \"url\": \"https://www.fortinet.com/resources/cyberglossary/social-engineering\" }"}}
