{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1588924746#6_3284445793","relevance":3,"reason":"The result is dedicated to baiting/social-engineering cybercrime and directly explains that scammers coerce unsuspecting users through curiosity, greed, fear, and emotions into actions that make them victims of cyberattacks, data breaches, or ransomware.","learned":"Cybercrime can appeal to victims by playing on curiosity, greed, fear, and other emotions so they rashly pick up devices, click, or otherwise expose themselves or their organization."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1993","reason":"The current query is still producing direct grade-3 evidence about phishing and social-engineering attacks using emotional triggers and appeals to manipulate victims, so continue for more relevant documents."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1993"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1480356709#15_3061719616","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1993","rank":11,"snippet":"Scam Websites What Are Scam Websites and How To Avoid Scam Websites What are scam website? How does a scam website work? How does a scam website exploit you? Types of scam websites Phishing Scam Websites Online Shopping Scam Websites Scareware Scam Websites Sweepstakes Scam Websites Examples of scam websites COVID-19 Vaccine Trial Scam Websites DMV <cover>Phishing Scam Websites How to identify fake websites How to avoid scam websites Check the domain name Be careful how you pay Too good to be true? Do an internet search Always use a secure connection What to do if you become a victim of a scam website How to report scam websites \" , \"segment\": \"Emotional language: Does the website speak in a way that may heighten your emotions? Proceed with caution if you feel an elevated level of urgency, </cover>optimism, or fear. Poor design quality: It may sound a little obvious but look closely at how a site is designed. Does it have the type of design skill and visual quality you would expect from a legitimate website? Low-resolution images and odd layouts can be a warning sign of a scam. Odd grammar: Look for things "}}
