{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_749830055#6_1726171159","relevance":3,"reason":"The result is dedicated to social engineering attack techniques and directly explains that baiting exploits a victim's greed or curiosity, luring victims into a trap to steal personal information or infect systems with malware.","learned":"Cybercrime can appeal to a victim by offering bait that attracts greed or curiosity, thereby luring the victim into malware infection or disclosure of personal information."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1994","reason":"This focused query produced direct grade-3 evidence about social-engineering lures appealing to greed and curiosity, so continue for more relevant documents within the remaining judgment budget."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1994"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_749830055#5_1726169046","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1994","rank":2,"snippet":"\"This is the biggest weakness that ‘social engineers’ exploit to trap victims! Some Common Social Engineering Attack Techniques Unscrupulous agents use different forms of social engineering attack techniques based on the gullibility of the target victim. The social engineering attack lifecycle consists of 4 basic steps – Investigation, Deception, Play and then Exit. Even a small point of human interaction is enough to execute a social engineering attack. The following sections shall enlighten you on the tips to avoid being a social engineering victim. But, before that, here are some common <cover>social engineering attack techniques. 1. Baiting This technique exploits the victim’s tendency to react to a bait that attracts his/her greed or curiosity. Miscreants lure victims </cover>into a trap with the intention of stealing their personal information or infecting their systems with malware. It is possible to execute baiting in both the physical as well as cyber space.\" , \"start_char\": 2325.000000 , \"title\": \"Top 5 Social Engineering Attack Techniques Used by Cyber Criminals\" , \"url\": \"https://ifflab.org/top-5-social-engineering-attack-techniques-used-by-cyber-criminals/\" }"}}
